    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-025: External CSS Loading** — load `<link rel=\"stylesheet\">` CSS, merge with inline `<style>`, parse as one stylesheet. First of a four-ADR arc (025→026→027→028) that closes the biggest remaining gap between \"HoneyBee renders HTML structure\" and \"HoneyBee renders what a browser renders.\"\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits) lands in a follow-up PR after this spec is reviewed and merged.\n\n## Grounded in measurement, not estimation\n\nFollowing the two Meta-lessons established by ADR-023/024: **measure the input distribution, and trace the code path, before predicting.**\n\n### Measured on Wikipedia's HTML article (2026-10-25)\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| HTML | 799,547 bytes |\n| `<link rel=\"stylesheet\">` tags | 2 |\n| External CSS | 222,927 bytes (216,046 + 6,881) |\n| ~CSS rules | 1,443 |\n| **Parser accepted** | **390 rules = 27.0%** |\n| **Rules using `var()`** | **255 of 323 accepted-with-var** |\n\n**Rule blockers (the 73% rejection):**\n\n| Construct | Rules blocked |\n|---|---|\n| `:not(...)` | 391 |\n| `:lang(...)` | 410 |\n| `::before`/`::after` | 98 |\n| `@media` blocks | 72 |\n| `@supports` blocks | 73 |\n| `[~=]`/`[^=]`/`[$=]`/`[*=]` | ~150 |\n\n**Skeleton coverage** (does the parsed 27% reach the structural classes?):\n\n| Class | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `.mw-parser-output` (article content) | ✅ **FOUND** (47 hits) |\n| `.infobox` | ✅ **FOUND** (36 hits) |\n| `body` | ✅ **FOUND** (partial) |\n| `.vector-menu` (sidebar) | ❌ MISSING |\n| `.vector-body` (content container) | ❌ MISSING |\n| `.vector-header` (top bar) | ❌ MISSING |\n| `.vector-toc` / `#toc` (table of contents) | ❌ MISSING |\n| `#bodyContent` | ❌ MISSING |\n| `.navbox` | ❌ MISSING |\n\n## The honest framing (baked into the ADR)\n\n**27% acceptance ≠ 27% visual improvement.** Two compounding reductions:\n\n1. **255 of the 323 var-using rules would parse but resolve to nothing** — CSS variables (`var(--x)`) aren't supported yet, so their declarations become no-ops. Effective visible rate ≈ 135 rules, ~9% of the total.\n\n2. **The structural classes are MISSING** — sidebar, header, TOC, article layout. Those rules exist and would improve things if parsed, but they're blocked by `@media` (72 blocks — likely wrapping the Vector skin rules) and `:root` (2 rules defining the 550 CSS variables).\n\n**So ADR-025 improves article-content styling** (references, infobox internals, code blocks, tables) — genuinely useful, but NOT \"Wikipedia looks like Wikipedia.\"\n\n## The four-ADR arc\n\nADR-025 is Phase 1 of 4. The ADR names all four explicitly:\n\n| ADR | Unlocks | Approx visible delta |\n|---|---|---|\n| **025** | External CSS loading | Article content styled (~25-35% of impression) |\n| **026** | `:root` + `var()` | 255 rules' values resolve (~15-20% more) |\n| **027** | `@media` blocks | Sidebar/header/TOC/layout activate (~30-40% more) |\n| **028** | `:not()` + attribute operators | Polish (~5-10%) |\n\nAfter ADR-028, Wikipedia looks like Wikipedia. After ADR-025 alone, it looks like a decent article reader with unstyled chrome.\n\n**Why external-CSS-first, not prerequisites-first:** prerequisites (var/@media/:not) have zero visible effect until CSS is loaded. Shipping them first would be three ADRs of \"nothing visible changed.\" External-CSS-first proves the fetch pipeline, delivers partial visual delta, and each subsequent ADR converts more of the loaded CSS.\n\n## Design decisions worth reviewing\n\n1. **Synchronous CSS fetch** in the navigation callback (~200-500ms added on Wikipedia). Async plumbing deferred. Combined caps: 10 stylesheets, 5s total. Fail-graceful per sheet.\n\n2. **Cache extends from string → `CacheEntry { html, external_css }`**. Back/Forward re-render from cache (no re-fetch — preserves ADR-020's promise). Reload re-fetches.\n\n3. **Merge external + inline CSS into one string, parse as one sheet**. Preserves source-order cascade. Multi-sheet support deferred to a media-query ADR.\n\n4. **Pipeline stays pure-transform** (no network I/O). Fetch lives in `window.cpp`; pipeline receives pre-fetched CSS via new `render_with_css(unique_ptr<Document>, string merged_css, float width)` API.\n\n5. **Entity-decoding gotcha documented**: Wikipedia's `<link href>` values are HTML-entity-encoded. Fetching the raw `&amp;`-encoded URL returned 196 bytes; the decoded URL returned 216KB. The ADR mandates verifying `get_attribute(\"href\")` decode behavior during implementation.\n\n## The escape hatch (ADR-021 → 022 → 023 → 024 pattern, applied prospectively)\n\nADR-025's Verification section includes an explicit **\"smaller-than-expected-delta\"** clause:\n\n> If <2 of 3 expected-YES visual sub-checks pass on Wikipedia after Commit 2, ship anyway (fetch pipeline is real value) but document the smaller delta and identify which blocker is dominant.\n\nThis is the honest-undershoot pattern that made ADR-022 → 023 → 024 work — but applied **at spec time**, not discovered during implementation.\n\n## Deferred (enumerated in ADR)\n\n- ADR-026: `:root` + `var()` (255 rules unlocked)\n- ADR-027: `@media` blocks (72 blocks — layout rules)\n- ADR-028: `:not()` + attribute operators (391 + 150 rules)\n- `::before`/`::after` (98 rules, needs pseudo-element render pipeline)\n- `@import`, async fetch, CORS, media-type filtering\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Is 27% + partial-visible-delta worth shipping?** My read: yes — fetch pipeline is real value, article content styling is real, and each follow-up ADR has 3x bigger payoff thanks to this one landing first.\n- [ ] **Is the four-ADR arc correctly scoped?** 025→026→027→028 — or should var()/@media be combined in one bigger ADR?\n- [ ] **Is synchronous fetch acceptable for v1?** 200-500ms extra navigation latency, vs ~80 lines of async plumbing deferred.\n- [ ] **Cache extension** — `CacheEntry { html, external_css }` is the right shape, or should it be a separate cache?\n- [ ] **Escape hatch policy** — \"ship at 27%, document honest delta, defer the rest to named ADRs\" — is this the right posture, or should ADR-025 stay blocked until var()/@media land first?\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. Will run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` after merge to confirm `main` still clean (271 cases, 1185 assertions, unchanged).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/025-external-css-loading.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #152\n",
